{
  "an9.22:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.22 ",
  "an9.22:0.2": "3. Abodes of Sentient Beings ",
  "an9.22:0.3": "A Wild Colt ",
  "an9.22:1.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you about three wild colts and three wild people; three excellent horses and three excellent people; and three fine thoroughbred horses and three fine thoroughbred people. ",
  "an9.22:1.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak. ",
  "an9.22:2.1": "And what are the three wild colts? ",
  "an9.22:2.2": "One wild colt is fast, but not beautiful or well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:2.3": "Another wild colt is fast and beautiful, but not well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:2.4": "While another wild colt is fast, beautiful, and well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:2.5": "These are the three wild colts. ",
  "an9.22:3.1": "And what are the three wild people? ",
  "an9.22:3.2": "One wild person is fast, but not beautiful or well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:3.3": "Another wild person is fast and beautiful, but not well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:3.4": "While another wild person is fast, beautiful, and well proportioned. ",
  "an9.22:4.1": "And how is a wild person fast, but not beautiful or well proportioned? ",
  "an9.22:4.2": "It’s when a mendicant truly understands: ‘This is suffering’ … ‘This is the origin of suffering’ … ‘This is the cessation of suffering’ … ‘This is the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering’. ",
  "an9.22:4.3": "This is how they’re fast, I say. ",
  "an9.22:4.4": "But when asked a question 